      <abstract id="aspace_be0dd6646cc9ca2a75cd2f1c57efede8" label="Abstract">The Schwabacher Company records in this collection include records of several of the enterprises in Seattle, the Stockton Milling Company in Stockton, California, and of Schwabacher Bros. of San Francisco. There were many Schwabacher brothers and cousins, involved in the many companies bearing their name.</abstract>
      <physloc id="aspace_f53b9036717978cd9c8c4b51b3f0b6b8" label="Collection Location">Special Collections and University Archives materials are stored offsite and must be paged three business days in advance. For more information on paging collections, see the department's website: https://library.stanford.edu/libraries/special-collections.</physloc>
      <langmaterial>
        <language langcode="eng">English</language>
      </langmaterial>
    </did>
    <scopecontent id="aspace_53d9a88f930094677769a1d00164ab1e">
      <head>Scope and Contents</head>
      <p>The records and papers in the collection cover the dates 1894-1944, and consist of miscellaneous reports and letters concerning the Seattle enterprises (1910 and 1921-1923); accountant's reports and balance sheets for each of the four Seattle companies represented (1910-1933); minute book and cash book, as well as sundry agreements and correspondence for the Stockton Milling Company (1894-1920); and checkbooks and a trial balance for Schwabacher Bros. in San Francisco (1906-1944).</p>
      <p>The Schwabacher company records in this collection include records of several of the enterprises in Seattle, the Stockton Milling Company in Stockton, California, and of Schwabacher Bros. of San Francisco. There were many Schwabacher brothers and cousins, involved in the many companies bearing their name. Following is a list of the companies represented in this collection and the member of the Schwabacher family apparently most closely connected with each:</p>
      <list type="ordered">
        <head>Missing Title</head>
        <item>Schwabacher Bros. of San Francisco: investment brokers - Louis A. Schwabacher</item>
        <item>Schwabacher Hardware Company, Seattle - Leo S. Schwabacher</item>
        <item>Schwabacher Bros. &amp; Co. Inc., Seattle - Abraham Schwabacher</item>
        <item>Schwabacher Realty Company, Seattle -</item>
        <item>Gatzert-Schwabacher Land Company, Seattle - Frank or Sigmund Schwabacher</item>
        <item>Stockton Milling Company-Stockton, California - Sigmund Schwabacher, president</item>
      </list>
    </scopecontent>
    <arrangement id="aspace_1ccec8e6d91bb8eca82304f4ca8c43a2">
      <head>System of Arrangement</head>
      <p>The collection is arranged into three series:
Series 1: Schwabacher Bros. of San Francisco, 1906-1944
Series 2: Seattle Enterprises, 1909-1933
Series 3: Stockton Milling Company, 1894-1920</p>
    </arrangement>
    <prefercite id="aspace_dc93246ccc2a36aaef1d75c72ae64842">
      <head>Preferred Citation</head>
      <p>[Identification of item] Schwabacher Company records (JL009), Department of Special Collections and University Archives, Stanford University Libraries, Stanford, Calif.</p>
    </prefercite>
    <custodhist id="aspace_5cd0f6a0f7d00eb50c383d3bc713cc71">
      <head>Provenance</head>
      <p>Gift of Sam I. Schwabacher, 1956.</p>
    </custodhist>
